<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ofu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ofu is a small volcanic island in the Manuʻa group of American Samoa, separated from neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olosega">Olosega</a> by a narrow channel now crossed by a bridge. Its south coast has coral reefs and a beach that form part of the National Park of American Samoa. Like the rest of Manuʻa, it was ceded to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1904.</p></div>
